      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5af6dccc56feb85f40087533|full_name}: You beat me to the upload! Although, for me those steps don't cause it 100% of the time. Last night I was able to cause it by adding an additional step and it happened 100% of the time this way. I was wondering why it still happened to me though when I had been avoiding doing what I do in my video. \n\n1. Hover your hand over an interactible object(which causes tooltips/glow/skeleton).\n2. While it's happening, open SteamVR via system button. \n3. In SteamVR's desktop view, click in and out and in. \n4. Press system button to be brought back into VRChat.\n\nVideo: \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AospS1mN_XE\n\nEdit for context: I'm on a Rift headset/Index controller hybrid set up.",
